<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Interpretability</title><link>https://jaehun.me/tags/interpretability/</link><description>딥러닝 컴파일러 엔지니어 류재훈의 기술 블로그. LLM 추론 최적화, KV 캐시, 컴파일러, C++와 AI 논문·오픈소스 코드 분석을 정리합니다.</description><language>ko-kr</language><atom:link href="https://jaehun.me/tags/interpretability/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Periodic Weak Spots: Phase Sensitivity from Chunked KV-Cache Compression</title><link>https://jaehun.me/posts/paper-2609-36322/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://jaehun.me/posts/paper-2609-36322/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0900</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a&#10; href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.36322"target="_blank"&#10; class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"&#10; &gt;논문 링크&lt;svg class="h-3 w-3 flex-shrink-0" id="external-link" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24"&gt;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 3h6v6m-11 5L21 3m-3 10v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="위상-감수성phase-sensitivity-청크-단위-kv-캐시-압축이-만드는-주기적-약점"&gt;위상 감수성(Phase Sensitivity): 청크 단위 KV 캐시 압축이 만드는 &amp;lsquo;주기적 약점&amp;rsquo;&lt;a href="#%ec%9c%84%ec%83%81-%ea%b0%90%ec%88%98%ec%84%b1phase-sensitivity-%ec%b2%ad%ed%81%ac-%eb%8b%a8%ec%9c%84-kv-%ec%ba%90%ec%8b%9c-%ec%95%95%ec%b6%95%ec%9d%b4-%eb%a7%8c%eb%93%9c%eb%8a%94-%ec%a3%bc%ea%b8%b0%ec%a0%81-%ec%95%bd%ec%a0%90" class="heading-anchor" aria-label="이 섹션에 대한 링크"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10; &lt;blockquote&#10; class="border-primary bg-muted/30 hover:bg-muted/40 my-6 rounded-r-lg border-l-4 py-4 pr-4 pl-6 italic transition-all duration-200 ease-out hover:translate-x-1"&#10; &gt;&#10; &lt;div class="prose prose-sm max-w-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR&lt;/strong&gt; — 청크 단위 KV 캐시 압축을 쓰는 모델(DeepSeek-V4 계열 등)에서, &lt;em&gt;같은 정보&lt;/em&gt;라도 압축 창 경계를 기준으로 한 &amp;lsquo;위상(phase)&amp;lsquo;에 따라 검색 성능이 최대 &lt;strong&gt;40pp&lt;/strong&gt;까지 주기적으로 달라진다. 평균 벤치마크 점수는 이 약점을 완전히 숨긴다.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>[논문리뷰]: Memory Retrieval and Consolidation in Large Language Models through Function Tokens</title><link>https://jaehun.me/posts/%EB%85%BC%EB%AC%B8%EB%A6%AC%EB%B7%B0-memory-retrieval-and-consolidation-in-large-language-models-through-function-tokens/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://jaehun.me/posts/%EB%85%BC%EB%AC%B8%EB%A6%AC%EB%B7%B0-memory-retrieval-and-consolidation-in-large-language-models-through-function-tokens/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 20 Dec 2025 00:00:00 +0900</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a&#10; href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.08203v1"target="_blank"&#10; class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"&#10; &gt;논문 링크&lt;svg class="h-3 w-3 flex-shrink-0" id="external-link" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24"&gt;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 3h6v6m-11 5L21 3m-3 10v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="function-token-hypothesis-llm-기억-검색의-게이트는-왜-구두점과-개행인가"&gt;Function Token Hypothesis: LLM “기억 검색”의 게이트는 왜 구두점과 개행인가&lt;a href="#function-token-hypothesis-llm-%ea%b8%b0%ec%96%b5-%ea%b2%80%ec%83%89%ec%9d%98-%ea%b2%8c%ec%9d%b4%ed%8a%b8%eb%8a%94-%ec%99%9c-%ea%b5%ac%eb%91%90%ec%a0%90%ea%b3%bc-%ea%b0%9c%ed%96%89%ec%9d%b8%ea%b0%80" class="heading-anchor" aria-label="이 섹션에 대한 링크"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2 id="한-줄-요약-tldr"&gt;한 줄 요약 (TL;DR)&lt;a href="#%ed%95%9c-%ec%a4%84-%ec%9a%94%ec%95%bd-tldr" class="heading-anchor" aria-label="이 섹션에 대한 링크"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;이 논문은 LLM의 기억을 “feature의 재활성화(retrieval) + 학습을 통한 feature 확장(consolidation)”으로 정의하고, &lt;strong&gt;function token&lt;/strong&gt;(고빈도 토큰)이 추론 시점에 예측에 필요한 feature들을 문맥-조건부로 재점화하며, 사전학습에서는&lt;strong&gt;function→content&lt;/strong&gt;예측이 최적화를 지배해 feature 수를 키운다는&lt;strong&gt;Function Token Hypothesis&lt;/strong&gt; 를 정량(coverage/degree)·정성(reactivation trace)·인과(steering)·학습동학(loss decomposition)으로 엮어 제시한다. (근거: §1, Fig.1, §3.1, Tab.1, §3.2, Fig.6, Fig.7, §4.2, Fig.8, §4.3, Fig.9)&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>[논문리뷰] Massive Activations in Large Language Models</title><link>https://jaehun.me/posts/%EB%85%BC%EB%AC%B8%EB%A6%AC%EB%B7%B0-massive-activations-in-large-language-models/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://jaehun.me/posts/%EB%85%BC%EB%AC%B8%EB%A6%AC%EB%B7%B0-massive-activations-in-large-language-models/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Jul 2025 00:00:00 +0900</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a&#10; href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.17762v2"target="_blank"&#10; class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"&#10; &gt;논문 링크&lt;svg class="h-3 w-3 flex-shrink-0" id="external-link" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24"&gt;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 3h6v6m-11 5L21 3m-3 10v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="massive-activations-hidden-biases-재해석된-self-attention의-비밀"&gt;Massive Activations, Hidden Biases: 재해석된 Self-Attention의 비밀&lt;a href="#massive-activations-hidden-biases-%ec%9e%ac%ed%95%b4%ec%84%9d%eb%90%9c-self-attention%ec%9d%98-%eb%b9%84%eb%b0%80" class="heading-anchor" aria-label="이 섹션에 대한 링크"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="한-줄-요약-tldr"&gt;한 줄 요약 (TL;DR)&lt;a href="#%ed%95%9c-%ec%a4%84-%ec%9a%94%ec%95%bd-tldr" class="heading-anchor" aria-label="이 섹션에 대한 링크"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;수천만 개 중 &lt;strong&gt;4–10 개의 초거대 스칼라(×10 000)&lt;/strong&gt; 가 LLM · ViT의 성능을 사실상 ‘혼자서’ 지탱한다.&#10;이 스칼라는 &lt;strong&gt;입력과 무관한 상수형 자기-어텐션 bias&lt;/strong&gt; 로 작동하며, -0-으로 만들면 모델이 즉시 붕괴(PPL → ∞)한다.&#10;저자들은 이 암묵적 현상을 &lt;strong&gt;Explicit Attention Bias(EAB)&lt;/strong&gt; 라는 모듈로 치환해 &lt;strong&gt;성능을 완전히 복구&lt;/strong&gt;하면서 분석·압축·안전성까지 한 번에 열어젖혔다.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>